WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.360
In 1950, India's new Constitution
abolished untouchability.

2
00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.830
Article 17 made its practice an offence.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:14.420
Yet discrimination in jobs, housing and
marriage is still a social issue today.

4
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.580
And manual scavenging,
cleaning waste by hand,

5
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.680
is still done mostly by
Dalits, despite being banned.

6
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.860
So if the law bans untouchability,
why is caste still debated,

7
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.010
and who gets to speak about it?

8
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:34.000
In this mission, you'll untangle two
words that are both translated as caste:

9
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.100
varna and jati.

10
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.880
Then you'll see how untouchability worked,

11
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.170
from separate wells to
closed temple doors.

12
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.900
Your mission: find out why
caste is still debated,

13
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.800
and who gets to speak about it.
